      "content": "That makes sense, the beating effect explains the \"wavering\" sensation quite well. \n\nMoving slightly away from the physics of it, I've been reading some older musicological texts that use much more colorful language to describe these phenomena. They sometimes refer to those sudden, irregular partials or the way a reed can produce these \"unwanted\" little chirps or rogue frequencies as being almost \"mischievous\" or having a \"will of their own.\" \n\nSince you brought up that comparison earlier, I'm curious—do you think there's any merit to describing these acoustic anomalies with that kind of personified language, or are you strictly viewing them as purely mechanical artifacts of the instrument's design?",
